00:49:10.260 --> 00:49:12.040
that's gotta be just an accident, right?

00:49:12.200 --> 00:49:13.120
Like there's no reason.

00:49:15.240 --> 00:49:16.700
There's no reason for that.

00:49:16.840 --> 00:49:18.180
Right. I don't know.

00:49:18.560 --> 00:49:21.280
Oh wait, another big change in the Famicom version.

00:49:21.280 --> 00:49:25.600
Sorry, I know I was about to talk about the TurboGrafx-16 thing, but this is a big update.

00:49:25.840 --> 00:49:27.220
The title screen's different.

00:49:27.440 --> 00:49:29.380
It's purple instead of blue.

00:49:29.380 --> 00:49:32.240
So, you know, kind of outrun vibes.

00:49:32.880 --> 00:49:37.880
And, uh, and they removed Michael up against the car.

00:49:38.220 --> 00:49:39.480
So it's just the car.

00:49:39.660 --> 00:49:41.640
It's just the car. They don't like Hasselhoff there.

00:49:41.780 --> 00:49:43.200
They're the anti-Germany.

00:49:43.440 --> 00:49:46.220
Yeah. I'm sure he felt very hassled by that.

00:49:48.300 --> 00:49:50.460
It's kind of like Back to the Future with no doc.

00:49:50.760 --> 00:49:53.320
You know, there's two major elements to your show and you just include one.

00:49:53.320 --> 00:49:58.580
Right, right. So anyway, back to the TurboGrafx-16 game.

00:49:58.820 --> 00:50:04.740
That is, again, almost the same game as the NES with the idea of just driving between cities and stuff.

00:50:04.780 --> 00:50:07.400
Except for now, they said, screw the cockpit view.

00:50:07.520 --> 00:50:09.360
Let's do third person perspective.

00:50:10.920 --> 00:50:12.800
Like, you're behind the car?

00:50:13.060 --> 00:50:15.000
Yeah, you're behind the entire car.

00:50:15.120 --> 00:50:17.800
Kind of like a Gran Turismo kind of view.

00:50:18.740 --> 00:50:20.880
I mean, like, that's been done.

00:50:20.880 --> 00:50:23.140
And so has the first person thing.

00:50:23.300 --> 00:50:29.960
But I think just looking at the ass of Kit is less cool than driving Kit.

00:50:30.860 --> 00:50:33.140
I never thought of it that I was looking at his ass.

00:50:33.240 --> 00:50:34.360
But you're right. Yeah.

00:50:35.160 --> 00:50:39.020
I wish I could pull up an image of Knight Rider Special for you two to just react to.

00:50:39.180 --> 00:50:41.680
But it's just great pixel work.

00:50:41.820 --> 00:50:43.980
But otherwise, it's nothing crazy.

00:50:44.140 --> 00:50:46.160
And I agree. I think that the cockpit view is better.

00:50:46.700 --> 00:50:47.640
I agree, too.

00:50:47.640 --> 00:50:55.100
I guess if I wanted to play Devil's Advocate, I mean, maybe they want people to be able to see the car.

00:50:55.360 --> 00:50:57.700
You know? Because it's a cool design car.

00:50:57.880 --> 00:51:00.200
It's like when you create a character in Skyrim.

00:51:00.280 --> 00:51:03.620
And then you play the next 80 hours of the game never looking at the character you created.

00:51:03.960 --> 00:51:05.660
So I guess I get that side of it.

00:51:05.720 --> 00:51:10.200
But I do agree that I think that it's just cooler to feel like you're behind the wheel.

00:51:10.200 --> 00:51:19.960
I will say, though, that most modern third-person games with this whole over-the-shoulder thing, less so than in older side-scrollers.

00:51:20.040 --> 00:51:24.360
You're really only looking at the back of a character's head most of the time.

00:51:24.760 --> 00:51:26.060
Sure. Yeah.

00:51:26.240 --> 00:51:31.120
And then there are two PlayStation 2 Knight Rider games, which is also just crazy to me.

00:51:31.260 --> 00:51:33.640
This one I did send you guys screenshots over to.

00:51:34.340 --> 00:51:37.240
You know, they look just exactly like you'd expect them to.

00:51:37.580 --> 00:51:40.180
Obviously, they're more open than any of these games.

00:51:40.380 --> 00:51:42.700
But it looks like you're stuck in the car this time.

00:51:43.240 --> 00:51:45.060
So really, it's funny that...

00:51:45.060 --> 00:51:46.660
Is that the plot point? No, no.

00:51:46.900 --> 00:51:48.860
Yeah, that's funny. I think it's just...

00:51:48.860 --> 00:51:56.100
It's interesting that the only Knight Rider game where you got out of the car and played as Michael, David Hasselhoff, was the very first game.

00:51:56.100 --> 00:51:57.800
And they were like, oh, people hated that.

00:51:57.800 --> 00:52:00.160
Like, people just want to be the car.

00:52:01.700 --> 00:52:09.340
And we'll find out if being the car is enough when we decide if this game is on the Essential Games list.

00:52:13.380 --> 00:52:15.380
Sean, is it enough to be the car?

00:52:16.980 --> 00:52:18.540
To drive the car?

00:52:18.760 --> 00:52:20.740
To be the... I think you are driving the car.

00:52:20.960 --> 00:52:22.700
You do see the dash. Yeah, you're definitely not Kit.

00:52:22.820 --> 00:52:23.920
You're not cool. You're not Kit.

00:52:25.520 --> 00:52:27.820
But is it enough to drive Kit?

00:52:29.180 --> 00:52:31.460
I do really like this game.

00:52:31.680 --> 00:52:39.360
I do think that the visuals are excellent for this sort of thing.

00:52:39.980 --> 00:52:46.180
The gameplay loop is, while not super...

00:52:48.360 --> 00:52:52.560
While it's not super complex, it is still fun.

00:52:53.920 --> 00:53:00.180
And the intermission breaks with the map and the conversations.

00:53:00.180 --> 00:53:01.260
Like, they're cool.

00:53:01.700 --> 00:53:04.080
And you got, like, your little list of cities.

00:53:04.080 --> 00:53:05.360
Like, going to all these cities.

00:53:05.560 --> 00:53:06.880
A lot of the...

00:53:08.040 --> 00:53:11.680
A lot of the presentational stuff is on point here.

00:53:12.820 --> 00:53:22.320
I will say, though, that it just doesn't have the it factor that, for me, makes it an essential game.

00:53:22.720 --> 00:53:26.920
I think that it's got a lot of good stuff going for it.

00:53:27.240 --> 00:53:29.440
But it's just not quite essential.

00:53:29.840 --> 00:53:30.680
Alright. Joe?

00:53:30.960 --> 00:53:34.680
Yeah, this was a lot better than I ever expected it to be.

00:53:34.740 --> 00:53:35.740
I'll say that for sure.

00:53:37.460 --> 00:53:40.980
I agree with Sean that the presentation is phenomenal.

00:53:41.280 --> 00:53:42.340
Also, I guess...

00:53:42.340 --> 00:53:44.740
Maybe it's just been a while since we played a game like this.

00:53:44.840 --> 00:53:49.340
But I was really, you know, impressed with how well it controls.

00:53:49.720 --> 00:53:50.940
So I thought that that was really cool.

00:53:51.140 --> 00:53:53.740
But ultimately, there's really not enough variety.

00:53:54.280 --> 00:53:56.080
I mean, there's a lot of variety in the imagery.

00:53:56.080 --> 00:54:01.640
And, like, some of the enemies, I guess.

00:54:01.820 --> 00:54:05.360
But, like, overall, the gameplay loop feels so much like a loop.

00:54:05.360 --> 00:54:07.020
It feels very repetitive to me.

00:54:07.920 --> 00:54:09.980
That I lose interest pretty quickly.

00:54:10.140 --> 00:54:13.260
I think this is a fun game to, like, pick up and play for a little bit.

00:54:14.520 --> 00:54:16.220
But not enough to kind of hold me.

00:54:16.380 --> 00:54:18.500
So I'm going to not vote it essential.

00:54:19.780 --> 00:54:21.600
I also had a lot of fun with this game.

00:54:21.600 --> 00:54:26.960
And I think I actually had a better time playing this game than I did watching the show it's based off of.

00:54:27.280 --> 00:54:30.240
So, you know, it's held up better than its own TV show.

00:54:30.380 --> 00:54:31.380
That's a pretty good statement.

00:54:32.320 --> 00:54:39.360
I think Joe was trying to talk about this earlier in the episode about just how smooth the gameplay is, too, though.

00:54:39.520 --> 00:54:41.860
Like, it doesn't feel choppy when you're driving.

00:54:41.860 --> 00:54:47.500
And I don't know if it's just the way they lock the background and not the highway.

00:54:47.500 --> 00:54:54.260
But, I don't know, I just felt like the driving experience was way better than I was giving you credit for throughout the episodes.

00:54:54.380 --> 00:54:57.960
I just want to, like, right that wrong if anybody thought that I didn't think that was impressive.

00:54:58.300 --> 00:55:02.400
But the other elements of the game are what make it less than.

00:55:02.540 --> 00:55:06.760
I kind of wonder what makes Kit so cool again.

00:55:06.920 --> 00:55:13.740
And not compared to his character on the show or, you know, personality or just, like, those kinds of things.

00:55:14.020 --> 00:55:15.940
But compared to other video game cars.

00:55:15.940 --> 00:55:19.840
Like, I don't know, it feels like every video game car could also just be secretly Kit.

00:55:20.100 --> 00:55:26.440
Because he does, he has, like, the same vulnerabilities and the same kinds of things that we've seen in other video games.

00:55:26.560 --> 00:55:31.860
And so, while his HUD was really cool and, you know, the presentation was top notch,

00:55:32.020 --> 00:55:40.600
I just didn't feel like, you know, playing as Michael and Kit was the definitive experience of a Knight Rider game.

00:55:40.600 --> 00:55:42.900
And so, it loses a little point there for me, too.

00:55:42.900 --> 00:55:43.900
So, not essential.

00:55:44.240 --> 00:55:45.940
You two already decided that.

00:55:46.060 --> 00:55:47.340
I'm just jumping in as well.

00:55:47.340 --> 00:55:56.660
But we've got another chance for a different intellectual property to be on the essential games list next week with RoboCop.

00:55:56.660 --> 00:56:03.160
So, it seems like everybody's just licensing everything they can get their hands on now as we kind of end out 1989.

00:56:03.660 --> 00:56:07.760
And who knows, because 1990 has so many more games than we've ever covered before.

00:56:08.100 --> 00:56:13.540
Maybe it's all just IPs and giant franchises and sequels of games.

00:56:13.540 --> 00:56:17.940
And we're going to think that, oh, will we ever see an original again?

00:56:20.240 --> 00:56:25.580
Are you intentionally giving us a taste of things to come right now, Mike?

00:56:26.040 --> 00:56:33.920
I think it's more to do with the fact that, like, we're thinking about that now in 2022, where we're like, oh, yeah, everything's a sequel.

00:56:34.480 --> 00:56:35.880
Everything is a reboot.

00:56:36.420 --> 00:56:38.460
We'll never, you know, original movies can't be made anymore.

00:56:38.580 --> 00:56:41.700
And, you know, now I'm kind of having the same thought in 1989.

00:56:43.740 --> 00:56:45.920
Yeah, maybe that's always what it feels like.

00:56:46.880 --> 00:56:49.820
Yeah, everything's based off of the success of something, right?

00:56:49.900 --> 00:56:51.580
Everything's based off the Odyssey, right, Sean?

00:56:54.060 --> 00:56:57.440
That is, yeah, that was the first and only story ever told.

00:56:58.120 --> 00:57:01.040
You know, it would be ridiculous if anyone on this podcast ever read that book.

00:57:01.160 --> 00:57:03.060
It would be absolutely insane.

